  "title": "CCEP ECoG dataset across age 4-51",
  "description": "This dataset contains cortico-cortical evoked potentials (CCEPs) recorded with electrocorticography (ECoG) during single pulse electrical stimulation in 74 patients aged 4-51 years. It was collected at the University Medical Center Utrecht as part of the RESPect epilepsy surgery registry and supports investigation of how signal transmission speed in the human brain develops with age. Data are organized in BIDS with electrode positions labeled by Destrieux atlas and transformed to MNI152 space.",
  "methods_description": "CCEPs were measured with ECoG during clinical single pulse electrical stimulation (SPES) in patients undergoing monitoring for epilepsy surgery. Electrode positions were localized on individual MRI, labeled with Destrieux atlas regions using Freesurfer, and converted to MNI152 space using a surface-based non-linear transformation.",
